# Forced phase oscillator on a torus: Arnold tongues
# x is the phase of an oscillator forced at frequency om, y is the phase of the forcing. Both are periodic (folded).
# Locked solutions satisfy x(T)=x(0)+2*pi*n and y(T)=y(0)+2*pi*m with T=2*pi*m/om; their edges in (om,b) are the tongues.
p(x)=-sin(x)/(1+a*cos(x))
x'=1+b*p(x)*cos(y)
y'=om
par om=2,b=.25,a=.25
init x=0,y=0
#@range om 0.5 3.2
#@range b 0 0.5
@ fold=x,fold=y,tor_per=6.283185
@ xp=x,yp=y,xlo=0,xhi=6.3,ylo=0,yhi=6.3
@ total=100,dt=0.05
done
